repository-code: "https://github.com/alexrvandam/Descriptron"
url: "https://github.com/alexrvandam/Descriptron"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "2.1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
abstract: >-
  Descriptron v2 turns images of specimens (photographs or micro-CT slices) into
  the outputs a taxonomist needs: measured structures, a character matrix, a
  dichotomous key, species delimitation, and formatted species treatments, with a
  record of how every number was obtained. Version 2 replaces the GPT-4o
  descriptions of version 1 with an evidence-tiered pipeline, BioRAG, in which the
  character matrix, the key, the delimitation and the audits are computed from the
  specimens, and a language model is used only to write prose from numbers it may
  not change. Retrieval is primarily from the measured data matrix (a per-species
  evidence sheet, the only source of numbers); published treatments of the group
  (BioSysLit on Zenodo and the user's own PDFs) are a secondary, optional source.
  Each treatment is audited independently of the model that wrote it:
  every statistic is recomputed from the specimen matrix, every number is
  attributed to a single feature, and every comparison is re-derived. Mask and
  landmark prediction include SAM2-PAL palindrome propagation, DINOLand (DINOv3
  landmark transfer) and torchvision detectors. Outputs include treatment
  documents, TaxPub XML, Darwin Core Archives, SDD and JSON-LD. The analysis needs
  no GPU, and the key, matrix, audits and delimitation need no language model.
keywords:
  - taxonomy
  - morphometrics
  - phenomics
  - species description
  - dark taxa
  - computer vision
